# Hexagonal Architecture

## GamesLibraryCore package (inside)

- Domain entities, value objects, errors
- Inbound ports (`*UseCasePort`) and outbound ports (`*RepositoryPort`)
- Use case implementations (pure orchestration, no I/O)

**Must NOT import:** SwiftUI, SwiftData, UIKit, HTTIES, BetterLogger, TTLCache, DIC, or any app/DTO type.

**May import:** Foundation only.

## GamesLibrary app target (outside)

- **Inbound adapters:** SwiftUI views, `@Observable` ViewModels, formatters, UI state enums
- **Outbound adapters:** repository implementations, DTOs (`Decodable`), mappers, cache, network
- **Composition root:** `AppContainer` wires dependencies; `AppCoordinator` handles navigation

## Rules

- ViewModels depend on inbound ports, never repositories or HTTP clients
- DTO-to-entity mappers live next to DTOs in `Infrastructure/Adapters/Outbound/`
- `#Preview` mocks the port, not the ViewModel
- Formatting (dates, ratings, HTML stripping) is a UI adapter concern
